<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sargon of Akkad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 2334 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/24th-century-bce">24th century BCE</a> · Also known as Sargon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sargon of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkad">Akkad</a> was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a>, whose reign is conventionally dated from c. 2334 BCE. Rising from obscure origins, he conquered the Sumerian city-states and created what is often called the first empire in history, ruling from the city of Akkad. Accounts of the Akkadian Empire credit him with a standing army and imperial administration, and accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamite-confederation">Elamite Confederation</a> record his campaigns against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sargon-of-akkad.jpg" alt="Sargon of Akkad" width="297" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ALFGRN · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sargon_of_Akkad_on_his_victory_stele.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
